WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.356
Let's walk through this proof: All horses are the same color.

00:00:04.356 --> 00:00:08.890
Base case: A single horse is always the same color as itself.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.490
Assume the property holds for n horses.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.210
In a set of n+1, the last

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.883
n horses are the same color.

00:00:18.883 --> 00:00:23.340
Application of inductive hypothesis to a subset of size n.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.644
The first n horses are also the same color.

00:00:27.644 --> 00:00:32.170
Application of inductive hypothesis to a different subset of size n.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:33.302
Wait!

00:00:33.302 --> 00:00:38.624
If n=1, there is no overlap between {h1} and {h2}!

00:00:38.624 --> 00:00:43.414
The overlap argument fails when n=1 (moving to n+1=2).

00:00:43.414 --> 00:00:49.801
For n=1, the first group is {h2} and the second is {h1}.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:53.527
There is no common horse to link

00:00:53.527 --> 00:00:56.720
the colors of h1 and h2.
